I have been noticing quite a few recent requests for a PC version
of NetHack.  A while ago I posted a notice that I have a copy of
PC-NetHack current to patchlevel 3.  However, since we are 
forced to limit ourselves to a smaller executable not all the 
options of unix NetHack have been enabled.  (The overlay version
of PC-NetHack is still in the testing stage and hopefully will be 
released in patch 6.  I am not the creator of the overlay version
so don't ask me any questions).
 
If you are in need of the executable it is available through the
following sources.
 
1)  You can email me your request and I can email you a copy, arc'ed,
    split, and uuencoded.
 
2)  You can slowmail me a disk and I will return it to you with the
    full executable and support files.
 
3)  You can login to the "Buffer Board" BBS here in Eugene, OR and 
    download it.  He will allow first time users to download.
 
4)  If there is a ftp site that would like to have it, I can send it
    there.  Just tell me where.
 
